  5485                                  ; ============================================================
  5486                                  ;  Aliases ("ali <name> <commands>")
  5487                                  ;
  5488                                  ;  An alias binds a name to an arbitrary command string (which may
  5489                                  ;  itself contain ; chains and a ~ pipe). Defining one is intercepted
  5490                                  ;  as raw text before ; splitting ever sees it (try_handle_ali_line,
  5491                                  ;  called from the interactive shell loop and from cmd_rr's script
  5492                                  ;  loop); invoking one happens inside dispatch, when cmd_buf doesn't
  5493                                  ;  match any built-in command but does match an alias name.
  5494                                  ; ============================================================
