  6916                                  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  6917                                  ;  disk_*: dispatcher in front of the two disk drivers below (legacy ATA
  6918                                  ;  PIO above, AHCI further down). Every caller in this file - vol_read,
  6919                                  ;  vol_write, dscan, fmt, mount - goes through these three routines with
  6920                                  ;  al = device id, exactly like it always called ata_select_device /
  6921                                  ;  ata_read_sector / ata_write_sector directly before. Ids 0-3 still mean
  6922                                  ;  what they always meant (primary/secondary x master/slave); ids 4 and up
  6923                                  ;  mean an AHCI port slot claimed by ahci_init at boot.
  6924                                  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
