  7033                                  ; pci_find_ahci: brute-force scan of PCI bus 0 only (per-device, and every
  7034                                  ; function of a multi-function device). This covers the common case - the
  7035                                  ; chipset's root complex, where AHCI controllers normally live, and is
  7036                                  ; where QEMU/Bochs/VirtualBox and most real desktop chipsets put theirs -
  7037                                  ; but doesn't walk PCI-to-PCI bridges out to other buses, which unusual
  7038                                  ; multi-bus hardware could need. Looks for class 0x01 (mass storage),
  7039                                  ; subclass 0x06 (SATA), regardless of programming interface.
