  7119                                  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  7120                                  ;  AHCI (SATA) driver. Talks to the HBA over MMIO (its ABAR, found via
  7121                                  ;  PCI BAR5) instead of legacy IDE ports - a different I/O model from the
  7122                                  ;  ata_* driver above, but the disk is identity-mapped memory either way
  7123                                  ;  once ahci_mark_uncached has run, so it's read/written with plain
  7124                                  ;  mov/or/and just like any other buffer in this file. No interrupts are
  7125                                  ;  used here either, matching the polled style of the rest of the OS:
  7126                                  ;  commands are issued and then polled for completion on PxCI.
  7127                                  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
