  7135                                  ; 512 entries each, 2MB pages). Without this, polling an HBA register
  7136                                  ; through a cacheable mapping could read back a stale value instead of
  7137                                  ; what the device just wrote - the ABAR sits in a dedicated MMIO range
  7138                                  ; that nothing else in this kernel uses, so marking its whole 2MB page
  7139                                  ; uncached doesn't affect anything else.
